  "label": "Adolf Hitler is mapped as 'this hero'",
  "description": "The text 'for this hero' at the bottom of the image explicitly maps the visual entity Adolf_Hitler onto the textual concept of a 'hero'. This is a direct analogical mapping where the historical figure is being reclassified or re-identified by the text as a 'hero', creating a hateful and ironic contrast with his actual role as the architect of genocide and the Holocaust. The mapping is established through the juxtaposition of the text with the visual material, where the text directly labels the person in the image.",
